$DIR/main.p:27:6: f was dropped by f.Drop() at line 26, so it can no longer be used here
    File is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when
    they are dropped. Calling Drop ends an owner's life: what f owned has been
    released.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    If this is the last use of f, move it before line 26, where f still holds
    its value.
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3301" for a longer explanation)
